{title: Wake Up}
{artist: NF}
Tuning: E A D G B E
{capo: 1st fret}

{start_of_bridge: Intro}
[Am]You spend your life in a dream that you can't escape
[F]Cause you live your life in a coma, you never awake
[Am]If you opened your eyes, then maybe you'd see what's at stake
[F]You're sleeping
[C]You're sleeping
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]You make a lot of money and you live in a mansion
[Am]And pretty much got everything that you could ever imagine
[F]But you feel like even though you got everything in the world
[F]You got nothing
[F]So what you do then is you start going backwards
[Am]You runnin' in a direction
[Am]And you lookin' for something that isn't real
[Am]And all you know is that you just gotta have it
[F]What you're doin' is sleepin'
[F]And thinking that you're awake and you're not
[F]And the problem is that you don't know what you're after
[Am]So you put everything that you have into what you do
[Am]Hoping that one day maybe you don't have to feel like you're empty
[F]But as you get older a lot of weight on your shoulders is getting heavy
[F]Then you look back and you start to regret things
[Am]You only get one life
[Am]And every time you lookin' at yours
[Am]You feel like everything you have is a waste!
[F]And the problem and the reason you could never fill a hole in your life
[F]Is because you were never awake
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus}

[Am]You spend your life in a dr[F]eam that you can't esc[Am]ape
Cause you li[C]ve your life in a c[F]oma, you're never a[C]wake
[Am]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
[F]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
[Am]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
[F]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]You wake up in the morning
[Am]But you feel like you never got up and go to work
[Am]And you feelin' like you ain't got a purpose
[F]And you tryna get motivated but everything you do turns into a mess
[F]Like you ain't nothing but worthless
[Am]And, yo, you look around
[Am]A lot of these other people you lookin' at
[Am]To you, you describe as perfect
[F]So you point a finger at God and tell him to do his job
[F]And fix ya' life up cause nothin' is workin'!
[Am]And you will try to hide and make it seem like it's nothin'
[Am]But really you feel like everything is crashin' around you
[F]And you develop a problem in trustin' in other people
[F]Which later became an issue that will mentally pound you!
[Am]You only get one life
[Am]But every time you lookin' at yours you feel like all you ever see are mistakes
[F]And the problem and the reason you could never move forward in life
[F]Is because you were never awake
[F]Wake up
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]You spend your life in a dr[F]eam that you can't esc[Am]ape
Cause you li[C]ve your life in a c[F]oma, you're never a[C]wake
[Am]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
[F]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
[Am]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
[F]Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!
{end_of_chorus}

